      <p>
        My journey in technology began with curiosity about how large distributed web services remain fast and dependable under massive concurrency. That fascination led me from writing basic algorithmic scripts in C and Python to architecting full-stack systems, containerized cloud pipelines, and open-source developer tooling.
      </p>
      <p>
        Currently, my primary focus spans <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">software engineering, distributed systems, and cloud infrastructure</span>. I enjoy dissecting internal runtime mechanics—whether that's understanding how Node.js flushes its microtask queue, how Docker configures cgroups and Linux namespaces, or how relational databases execute multi-table joins.
      </p>
      <p>
        When I am not writing code or studying for university coursework, I document my architectural experiments on my blog, contribute to open-source software, and mentor junior computer science students.
      </p>
